nment": 8.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.39}, "rating_margin": -15.22, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.83, "baseline_margin": -10.81, "analyst_adjustment": -3.19, "key_factors": ["Strong Republican district (R+11 PVI) in an open seat", "Alfonso's large fundraising and outside-spending edge over Clark", "All nine expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe R", "Markets price a Democratic win at only about 5%"], "rationale": "The R+11 partisan lean, Alfonso's roughly three-to-one cash advantage plus $2.2 million in outside support, and a unanimous Solid/Safe R expert consensus all point to a comfortable Republican hold of Tiffany's open seat. The margin is set slightly beyond the fundamentals because ratings and money reinforce the district's lean.", "watch": "Alfonso's comment on raising the voting age and his debate absence could create an opening, but only a major scandal or wave would put the seat in play.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Tom Tiffany (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Tom Tiffany's retirement leaves this northern Wisconsin seat open, but the district's R+11 lean keeps it firmly in Republican hands on paper. Michael Alfonso, who won a contested GOP primary with family ties to a well-known political network, enters the general with a major financial edge: about $1.35 million raised, $663,000 on hand, and $2.25 million in outside support. Democrat Fred Clark has run an active campaign with town halls across the district but has raised only about $423,000 and drawn no outside spending.\n\nNo public general-election polling exists, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings and markets. Every major rater calls the race Solid or Safe Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 5% chance. Alfonso's refusal to debate and his comment on raising the voting age are the only visible friction points, but they are unlikely to overcome the district's strong Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0554, "margin": -10.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0215, "margin": -14.0}]}